.TH GIRLC 1 2026-10-14 girlpages "girlpages Manual"
.SH NAME
girlc \- read girly man pages from a girlpages repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B girlc
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ section ]
.IR page \ ...
.br
.B girlc
.B \-k
.RI [ options ]
.IR words \ ...
.br
.B girlc
.B \-f
.IR page \ ...
.br
.B girlc
.B \-\-versions
.IR page \ ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B girlc
reads man pages, girlified by
.BR girl (1),
straight from a girlpages repository (published by
.BR girlrepo (1)),
the way
.BR man (1)
reads them from the system.
Nothing needs to be installed but
.B girlc
itself: no model, no cache, and no man pages; it reads any page the
repository has, in any version and variant.
.PP
Pages are named as for
.BR man :
.RI [ section ]
.IR page ,
or
.IR page ( section ),
and
.B rfc
.I number
(or
.BI rfc number\fR)
for an RFC.
A page named alone is the first by
.BR man 's
section order (1, n, l, 8, 3, 0, 2, 5, 4, 9, 6, 7, and a section's
extensions after it: 3 before 3p), in any case, as
.B man
finds them.
.PP
Pages are shown girlified, in a pager if standard output is a terminal.
If the latest version of a page isn't girlified yet, its original is shown,
with a note saying which version is, if any.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show every page by the name, not just the first.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-S ", " \-\-sections =\fIlist\fR
Only look in these sections (separated by colons or commas).
As with
.BR man ,
.B 3
includes
.BR 3p ,
.B 3ssl
and so on.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-apropos
Search the repository, as
.BR apropos (1)
searches the system: for each argument, by the words in pages' names,
descriptions and text (a quoted argument of several words finds pages with
all of them first), best first, as
.B name (section) \- description
lines.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-whatis
Show the one-line description of every page by each name, as
.BR whatis (1)
does.
.TP
.B \-\-ngrams
With
.BR \-k ,
also find words inside other words
.RB ( dir
finds
.B mkdir
and
.BR readdir ).
.TP
.BR \-\-limit =\fIn\fR
How many pages
.B \-k
lists for each search (default 100; 0 for all).
.TP
.BR \-\-page\-version =\fIversion\fR
Which version of a page to read: its version number
.RB ( 9.7 ),
where it's from
.RB ( debian ", " debian/trixie
or
.BR "debian trixie" ,
for the latest from there), or the start of its source hash.
The default is the latest.
.TP
.BR \-\-variant =\fIname\fR
Which variant to read:
.B girl
(the default),
.B man
(the original) or any other the repository has.
.TP
.B \-\-versions
List a page's versions, with how to pick each, where it's from, and its
variants, instead of reading it.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Print the page as it's stored (girlpages markup, or plain text for
originals) instead of rendering it.
.TP
.BR \-\-color =\fIwhen\fR
.BR auto " (the default: if standard output is a terminal), " always " or " never .
.B NO_COLOR
turns it off.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-pager =\fIpager\fR
Page output with
.I pager
(default
.BR $GIRLPAGER ,
.BR $PAGER ,
then
.BR less ).
.TP
.BR \-\-repo =\fIurl\fR
The repository to read: an http(s) URL, a
.B file://
URL or a directory, either the repository itself or a site with it in
.BR repo/ .
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-config\-file =\fIfile\fR
Read this configuration file instead of the user's.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B girlc
reads
.BR girl 's
configuration files (see
.BR girl (1)),
for the repository, its timeout and the pager:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pager = ""

[repo]
url = "https://example.org/repo"
timeout = "20s"
.fi
.RE
.PP
The repository is the one given with
.BR \-\-repo ,
else
.B url
from the configuration, else the one
.B girlc
was built with (set by packagers with
.BR "make girlc GIRLC_REPO=" \fIurl\fR).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGER ", " PAGER
The pager, if
.B \-P
and
.B pager
aren't set.
.TP
.B MANWIDTH
The width to render pages at (by default the terminal's, up to 100).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/girlpages/config.toml
System configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/girlpages/config.toml
User configuration.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
The repository couldn't be read.
.TP
.B 16
A page was not found, or a search found nothing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B girlc ls
Show
.BR ls (1).
.TP
.B girlc 3 printf
Show
.BR printf (3)
rather than
.BR printf (1).
.TP
.B girlc \-a printf
Show every
.BR printf :
1, 3 and 3p.
.TP
.B girlc \-k \(dqlist directory\(dq
Find pages about listing directories.
.TP
.B girlc \-\-versions ls
.PD 0
.TP
.B girlc \-\-page\-version debian/bookworm \-\-variant man ls
.PD
See which versions of
.BR ls (1)
the repository has, then read the original of Debian bookworm's.
.TP
.B girlc \-\-repo https://example.org rfc 9110
Read RFC 9110 from another repository.
